{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Admin-only, read-only WebDAV adapter for mounting a PEER's share: /files/peerdav/<peer uuid>/<path> on THIS instance speaks DAV to the local mount client (rclone, davfs2) and translates each request into peer-network calls, so nothing leaves the encrypted peer channel and the core peer proxy is not involved. OPTIONS answers locally (Allow: OPTIONS, PROPFIND, GET, HEAD). PROPFIND (Depth 0/1) runs the peer's files.propfind through peer.service.exec with href_prefix /files/peerdav/<uuid>, so hrefs point back at this mount. GET/HEAD first run a Depth 0 PROPFIND (404, collection -> 405, Content-Length and type), then GET asks the peer's peer.peer.local for /files/get_file and joins the returned peer stream as the response body. No Range support. PUT/MKCOL/DELETE/COPY/MOVE answer 403 (read-only). The peer authorizes with its own groups: the caller must be in the peer's files group (403 otherwise); unreachable peers answer 504, other peer failures 502. uuid `local` is a loopback onto this instance's own share for the test harness.","import":"use crate::files::files::get_file::get_file;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse std::panic::{catch_unwind, AssertUnwindSafe};","params":[{"desc":"HTTP request method supplied by app.service.init.","name":"nn_method","type":"String"},{"desc":"Raw request path: /files/peerdav/<peer uuid>/<share-relative path>.","name":"nn_path","type":"String"},{"desc":"HTTP request headers supplied by app.service.init.","name":"nn_headers","type":"JSONObject"},{"desc":"Raw HTTP request bytes supplied by app.service.init for non-POST requests (the PROPFIND XML).","name":"nn_body","type":"Any"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"jpknvu1a1c8192cb7n1","readers":[],"time":1794358906162,"username":"system","writers":[]}